.TH MCP-SERVER-FILESYSTEM 1 "August 2026" "mcp-server-filesystem" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcp-server-filesystem \- MCP server exposing Linux filesystem operations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcp-server-filesystem
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mcp-server-filesystem
is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that exposes Linux filesystem
operations as tools for an LLM agent.
It communicates over stdio using the MCP protocol and is intended to be
launched by an MCP client (e.g. Claude Code, Claude Desktop, mcprack, or
any other MCP-compatible agent runtime), not run interactively.
.PP
It is built on
.BR fastmcp .
.SH TOOLS
.SS Read-only
.TP
.B list_dir(path=".")
List the contents of a directory.
.TP
.B read_file(path, encoding="utf-8", binary=False, max_bytes=1048576)
Read a file's contents.
.TP
.B stat(path)
Fetch filesystem metadata for a path.
.TP
.B exists(path)
Check whether a path exists.
.TP
.B glob_search(pattern, path=".")
Search for files matching a glob pattern.
.SS Mutating (require FS_READONLY=false)
.TP
.B write_file(path, content, encoding="utf-8", append=False)
Write text content to a file.
.TP
.B mkdir(path, parents=True, exist_ok=True)
Create a directory.
.TP
.B delete(path, recursive=False)
Delete a file or directory.
.TP
.B move(src, dst)
Move/rename a file or directory.
.TP
.B copy(src, dst, recursive=False)
Copy a file or directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FS_ROOT
Directory all paths are confined to (default: current working directory).
.TP
.B FS_READONLY
.B true
(default) blocks mutating tools;
.B false
allows writes/deletes/moves.
